IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `rra-nouns`
IMPORT `rra-logic`
IMPORT `rra-part1-preliminary`

-- Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal
-- consolidation in force from 1 July 2022 -- PART 3 RE-EMPLOYMENT OF ELIGIBLE EMPLOYEES (ss 7 to 7C).
--
-- Answers are MAYBE BOOLEAN: JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE where the text itself says yes / no (the words quoted at that branch),
-- NOTHING where it does not (tagged `NOTHING-kind (...)`).  Judgments the Act hands to the employer, the Minister or the
-- Tribunal are inputs.  Where a duty has a time limit the Act states, the duty is also written as a regulative rule, run
-- with #TRACE in the tests; a DEONTIC cannot be the operand of #ASSERT on a main build, so the same duty is asserted as a
-- decision function.

§ `Part 3 -- Re-employment of eligible employees`

§§ `Section 7 -- Re-employment eligibility criteria`

-- src:311 | (a) the employee is born on or after 1 July 1952; and
@ref s 7(1)(a) (src:311)
GIVEN `the date of birth` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(1)(a) the employee is born on or after 1 July 1952` MEANS
    IF `the date of birth` AT LEAST (Date 1 7 1952)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an employee is eligible for re-employment in accordance with section 7A if (a) the employee is born on or after 1 July 1952" -- a failed "if" (marginal reading (a))
        JUST FALSE

-- The employer's presumption: see section 7(2) below.  The employer's assessment of the employee's work performance
-- is the employer's judgment and is an input: JUST TRUE (assessed at least satisfactory), JUST FALSE (assessed less),
-- NOTHING (not assessed, or not known to the person asking).
-- src:318 | (b) the employer assesses the employee as —
-- src:320 | (i) having at least satisfactory work performance; and
-- src:322 | (ii) being medically fit to continue working.
@ref s 7(1)(b)(ii) (src:318-322)
GIVEN `the employer has proved on a balance of probabilities that the employee is not medically fit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(1)(b)(ii) the employee counts as assessed by the employer as medically fit to continue working` MEANS
    `s 7(2) the employee is presumed to be medically fit to continue working` `the employer has proved on a balance of probabilities that the employee is not medically fit`

-- src:309 | 7.—(1) For the purposes of this Act, an employee is eligible for
-- src:310 | re-employment in accordance with section 7A if —
@ref s 7(1) (src:309-310)
GIVEN `the date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the employer assesses the employee as having at least satisfactory work performance` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the employer has proved on a balance of probabilities that the employee is not medically fit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(1) the employee is eligible for re-employment in accordance with section 7A` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an employee is eligible for re-employment in accordance with section 7A if" (a) and (b)(i) and (b)(ii) -- a failed limb of an "if" (marginal reading (a))
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the employer's assessment of the employee's work performance is the employer's judgment and is not among the sources; where it is not known and no other limb fails, the answer is not known
    `every one of these answers is yes`
        (LIST `s 7(1)(a) the employee is born on or after 1 July 1952` `the date of birth`
            , `the employer assesses the employee as having at least satisfactory work performance`
            , `s 7(1)(b)(ii) the employee counts as assessed by the employer as medically fit to continue working` `the employer has proved on a balance of probabilities that the employee is not medically fit`)

-- "eligible employee" means an employee who satisfies the re-employment eligibility criteria set out in section 7(1).
-- It is written here, in the module of the section it points at, so that it can call section 7(1).
-- src:130 | “eligible employee” means an employee who satisfies the
-- src:131 | re-employment eligibility criteria set out in section 7(1);
@ref s 2(1) "eligible employee" (src:130-131)
GIVEN `the person is an employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the employer assesses the employee as having at least satisfactory work performance` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the employer has proved on a balance of probabilities that the employee is not medically fit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "eligible employee" the person is an eligible employee` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“eligible employee” means an employee who satisfies the re-employment eligibility criteria set out in section 7(1)"
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): see section 7(1): the employer's assessment is not among the sources
    `every one of these answers is yes`
        (LIST JUST `the person is an employee`
            , `s 7(1) the employee is eligible for re-employment in accordance with section 7A` `the date of birth` `the employer assesses the employee as having at least satisfactory work performance` `the employer has proved on a balance of probabilities that the employee is not medically fit`)

-- src:326 | (2) For the purpose of subsection (1)(b)(ii), an employee is
-- src:327 | presumed to be medically fit to continue working, unless the
-- src:328 | employer of the employee proves, on a balance of probabilities,
-- src:329 | that the employee is not medically fit.
@ref s 7(2) (src:326-329)
GIVEN `the employer has proved on a balance of probabilities that the employee is not medically fit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(2) the employee is presumed to be medically fit to continue working` MEANS
    IF `the employer has proved on a balance of probabilities that the employee is not medically fit`
    THEN
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an employee is presumed to be medically fit to continue working, unless the employer of the employee proves, on a balance of probabilities, that the employee is not medically fit"
        JUST FALSE
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- Section 7(3): where the employer does not intend to re-employ because the employee does not meet the criteria in
-- section 7(1)(b), it must, as far as it is reasonably practicable, give written notice of that intention within a
-- reasonable period before terminating the employee's employment.  "Reasonably practicable" and "a reasonable period" are
-- the person's judgments and are inputs.
-- src:331 | (3) Where an employer does not intend to re-employ an employee
-- src:332 | because the employee does not meet the criteria in subsection (1)(b),
-- src:333 | then as far as it is reasonably practicable, the employer must give the
-- src:334 | employee written notice of that intention within a reasonable period
-- src:335 | before terminating the employee’s employment.
@ref s 7(3) (src:331-335)
GIVEN `the employer does not intend to re-employ the employee because the employee does not meet the criteria in section 7(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is reasonably practicable for the employer to give written notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer gave the employee written notice of that intention` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice was given within a reasonable period before terminating the employee's employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(3) the employer has complied with the duty to give written notice of the intention not to re-employ` MEANS
    IF NOT `the employer does not intend to re-employ the employee because the employee does not meet the criteria in section 7(1)(b)`
    THEN
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty arises "where an employer does not intend to re-employ an employee because the employee does not meet the criteria in subsection (1)(b)"
        NOTHING
    ELSE IF NOT `it is reasonably practicable for the employer to give written notice`
         THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is owed "as far as it is reasonably practicable"; where giving notice was not reasonably practicable the section does not say what is owed
            NOTHING
         ELSE IF `the employer gave the employee written notice of that intention` AND `the notice was given within a reasonable period before terminating the employee's employment`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE
                -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the employer must give the employee written notice of that intention within a reasonable period before terminating the employee's employment" -- a requirement not met (marginal reading (a))
                JUST FALSE

-- The duty as a regulative rule.  Section 7(3) states no number of days ("a reasonable period before terminating"), so the
-- rule carries no WITHIN: it stands until the notice is given.
@ref s 7(3) (src:331-335)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`s 7(3) the employer must give the employee written notice of the intention not to re-employ` MEANS
    PARTY Employer
    MUST `give the employee written notice of the intention not to re-employ`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Employer BECAUSE "s 7(3): the employee was not given written notice of the intention not to re-employ"

§§ `Section 7A -- Employer to re-employ eligible employee`

-- Section 7A(1) is "Subject to section 7C": where section 7C(1) disapplies section 7A, there is no duty to offer.  That
-- no is section 7C(1)'s ("Section 7A does not apply if ..."); this rule carries it, as the section it is subject to.
-- src:341 | 7A.—(1) Subject to section 7C, an employer must, before an
-- src:342 | employee of the employer (being an eligible employee) attains the
-- src:343 | specified age, offer re-employment to that employee and the
-- src:344 | employer’s obligation to re-employ that employee begins from the
-- src:345 | time that employee attains the specified age, until that employee
-- src:346 | attains the employee’s prescribed re-employment age.
@ref s 7A(1) (src:341-346)
GIVEN `the employee is an eligible employee` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `section 7A does not apply to the employer under section 7C(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7A(1) the employer owes the employee an offer of re-employment before the specified age` MEANS
    IF `section 7A does not apply to the employer under section 7C(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Section 7A does not apply if an employer ... is unable to re-employ an eligible employee" (section 7C(1)), to which section 7A(1) is "Subject"
        JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the employee is an eligible employee` EQUALS JUST FALSE
         THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the duty is owed to "an employee of the employer (being an eligible employee)", and section 7(1) has already said no: "an employee is eligible for re-employment in accordance with section 7A if" its limbs are met (fork F19, marginal reading (a))
            JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF `the employee is an eligible employee` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `section 7A does not apply to the employer under section 7C(1)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE
                -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the employee's eligibility, or whether section 7C(1) takes the duty away, is not known
                NOTHING

-- "before an employee ... attains the specified age": the last day for the offer is the day before.
@ref s 7A(1) (src:341-346)
GIVEN employment IS AN Employment
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 7A(1) the last day on which the employer can offer re-employment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 2(3) the date of the anniversary on which the person attains the age` (employment's `date of birth`) (`s 2(1) "specified age" the employee's specified age` employment)
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the date on which the employee attains the specified age cannot be worked out (29 February birth, no anniversary date)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST attained THEN JUST (attained MINUS 1)

@ref s 7A(1) (src:341-346)
GIVEN employment IS AN Employment
      `the date the offer was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7A(1) the offer of re-employment was made before the employee attained the specified age` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 7A(1) the last day on which the employer can offer re-employment` employment
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the date on which the employee attains the specified age cannot be worked out (29 February birth, no anniversary date)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST last THEN
        IF `the date the offer was made` AT MOST last
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an employer must, before an employee of the employer (being an eligible employee) attains the specified age, offer re-employment to that employee" -- a requirement not met (marginal reading (a))
            JUST FALSE

-- "the employer's obligation to re-employ that employee begins from the time that employee attains the specified age,
-- until that employee attains the employee's prescribed re-employment age": the obligation is on foot from the date
-- the specified age is attained up to, but not including, the date the prescribed re-employment age is attained (fork F6).
@ref s 7A(1) (src:341-346)
GIVEN employment IS AN Employment
      `the employee is an eligible employee` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `section 7A does not apply to the employer under section 7C(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7A(1) the employer's obligation to re-employ the employee is on foot on the date` MEANS
    IF `section 7A does not apply to the employer under section 7C(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Section 7A does not apply if an employer ... is unable to re-employ an eligible employee" (section 7C(1)), to which section 7A(1) is "Subject"
        JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the employee is an eligible employee` EQUALS JUST FALSE
         THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the obligation is owed to "an employee of the employer (being an eligible employee)", and section 7(1) has already said no: "an employee is eligible for re-employment in accordance with section 7A if" its limbs are met (fork F19, marginal reading (a))
            JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF NOT (`the employee is an eligible employee` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `section 7A does not apply to the employer under section 7C(1)` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
              THEN
                -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the employee's eligibility, or whether section 7C(1) takes the duty away, is not known
                NOTHING
              ELSE
                CONSIDER `s 2(3) the date of the anniversary on which the person attains the age` (employment's `date of birth`) (`s 2(1) "specified age" the employee's specified age` employment)
                -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the date on which the employee attains the specified age cannot be worked out (29 February birth, no anniversary date)
                WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
                WHEN JUST began THEN
                    CONSIDER `s 2(3) the date of the anniversary on which the person attains the age` (employment's `date of birth`) (employment's `prescribed re-employment age`)
                    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the date on which the employee attains the prescribed re-employment age cannot be worked out (29 February birth, no anniversary date)
                    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
                    WHEN JUST ended THEN
                        IF `the date asked about` AT LEAST began AND `the date asked about` LESS THAN ended
                        THEN JUST TRUE
                        ELSE
                            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the obligation runs "from the time that employee attains the specified age, until that employee attains the employee's prescribed re-employment age"; the date is outside that period
                            NOTHING

-- The duty to offer, as a regulative rule.  The clock counts days from `the day the clock starts`, which must be before
-- the day the employee attains the specified age.  The offer is due by the day before that day, inclusive.
@ref s 7A(1) (src:341-346)
GIVEN `the day the employee attains the specified age` IS A DATE
      `the day the clock starts` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`s 7A(1) the employer must offer re-employment before the employee attains the specified age` MEANS
    PARTY Employer
    MUST `offer re-employment`
    WITHIN (Day `the day the employee attains the specified age` MINUS Day `the day the clock starts` MINUS 1)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Employer BECAUSE "s 7A(1): re-employment was not offered before the employee attained the specified age"

-- src:352 | (2) Where —
-- src:354 | (a) an employee mentioned in section 7(1)(a) continues, after
-- src:355 | attaining the specified age, to work for his or her employer;
-- src:356 | and
-- src:358 | (b) the employer does not, upon that employee attaining the
-- src:359 | specified age —
-- src:361 | (i) re-employ that employee; or
-- src:363 | (ii) terminate the employment of that employee,
-- src:365 | then any right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or
-- src:366 | incurred by the employee under the contract of service between the
-- src:373 | employee and his or her employer before the employee attains the
-- src:374 | specified age is not affected.
@ref s 7A(2) (src:352-374)
GIVEN `the employee is born on or after 1 July 1952` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee continues, after attaining the specified age, to work for the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer re-employs the employee upon the employee attaining the specified age` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer terminates the employment upon the employee attaining the specified age` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7A(2) a right, privilege, obligation or liability accrued before the specified age is affected` MEANS
    IF `the employee is born on or after 1 July 1952` AND `the employee continues, after attaining the specified age, to work for the employer` AND (NOT `the employer re-employs the employee upon the employee attaining the specified age`) AND (NOT `the employer terminates the employment upon the employee attaining the specified age`)
    THEN
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred by the employee under the contract of service ... before the employee attains the specified age is not affected"
        JUST FALSE
    ELSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence begins "Where" an employee mentioned in section 7(1)(a) continues to work after the specified age and the employer neither re-employs nor terminates; the case falls outside
        NOTHING

§§ `Section 7A(3) -- the employer who neither re-employs nor terminates`

-- "(a) may, at any time after the employee ... has attained the specified age -- (i) re-employ the employee": a grant.
-- Where the conditions of the grant are not met, the text does not say the employer may not (limited by its own wording).
-- src:378 | (3) Where subsection (2) applies, the employer referred to in that
-- src:379 | subsection —
-- src:381 | (a) may, at any time after the employee referred to in that
-- src:382 | subsection has attained the specified age —
-- src:384 | (i) re-employ the employee; or
@ref s 7A(3) (src:378-384)
GIVEN `subsection (2) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee has attained the specified age` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7A(3) the employer may re-employ the employee` MEANS
    IF `subsection (2) applies` AND `the employee has attained the specified age`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is for "the employer referred to in" subsection (2), "at any time after the employee ... has attained the specified age"; the case falls outside
        NOTHING

-- "(ii) terminate the employment of the employee if the employee does not satisfy the eligibility criteria set out in
-- section 7(1)(b)": the grant is limited by an "if" to an employee who fails section 7(1)(b); within the case subsection (3)
-- speaks to ("Where subsection (2) applies", "at any time after ... the specified age"), an employee who satisfies
-- section 7(1)(b) fails that "if", and the answer is no (fork F20).  Outside that case the section is silent.
-- src:378 | (3) Where subsection (2) applies, the employer referred to in that
-- src:379 | subsection —
-- src:381 | (a) may, at any time after the employee referred to in that
-- src:382 | subsection has attained the specified age —
-- src:386 | (ii) terminate the employment of the employee if the
-- src:387 | employee does not satisfy the eligibility criteria set
-- src:388 | out in section 7(1)(b); and
@ref s 7A(3) (src:378-388)
GIVEN `subsection (2) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee has attained the specified age` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee satisfies the eligibility criteria set out in section 7(1)(b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7A(3) the employer may terminate the employment of the employee` MEANS
    IF `subsection (2) applies` AND `the employee has attained the specified age` AND `the employee satisfies the eligibility criteria set out in section 7(1)(b)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `subsection (2) applies` AND `the employee has attained the specified age` AND `the employee satisfies the eligibility criteria set out in section 7(1)(b)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the employer may "terminate the employment of the employee if the employee does not satisfy the eligibility criteria set out in section 7(1)(b)"; the employee does satisfy them, so the "if" is not met and the permission does not arise (fork F20, marginal reading (a))
            JUST FALSE
         ELSE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is for "the employer referred to in" subsection (2), "at any time after" the specified age; the case falls outside it, or whether the employee satisfies section 7(1)(b) is not known
            NOTHING

-- "(b) is deemed to have complied with the requirement under subsection (1) for the period between (i) the time the
-- employee attains the specified age; and (ii) the time the employer re-employs the employee or terminates the
-- employment": both ends are read as inside the period (fork F17).  Before the employer re-employs or terminates, the
-- period has no end yet and runs on.
-- src:390 | (b) is deemed to have complied with the requirement under
-- src:391 | subsection (1) for the period between —
-- src:393 | (i) the time the employee attains the specified age; and
-- src:395 | (ii) the time the employer re-employs the employee or
-- src:396 | terminates the employment of the employee under
-- src:397 | paragraph (a).
@ref s 7A(3) (src:390-397)
GIVEN `subsection (2) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the employee attains the specified age` IS A DATE
      `the date the employer re-employs or terminates` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7A(3) the employer is deemed to have complied with section 7A(1) on the date` MEANS
    IF NOT `subsection (2) applies`
    THEN
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the deeming is for "the employer referred to in" subsection (2); subsection (2) does not apply
        NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the date asked about` LESS THAN `the date the employee attains the specified age`
         THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the deeming runs "for the period between" the specified age and the re-employment or termination; the date is before that period
            NOTHING
         ELSE
            CONSIDER `the date the employer re-employs or terminates`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN JUST ended THEN
                IF `the date asked about` AT MOST ended
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE
                    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the deeming runs "for the period between" the specified age and the re-employment or termination; the date is after that period
                    NOTHING

§§ `Section 7A(4) to (7) -- the re-employment contract`

-- src:401 | (4) For the purposes of re-employment under subsection (1) or
-- src:402 | (3)(a)(i), a re-employment contract must be entered into by the
-- src:403 | employee and his or her employer, in which the job scope and the
-- src:404 | terms and conditions may vary from those in the previous contract of
-- src:405 | service between them.
@ref s 7A(4) (src:401-405)
GIVEN `the re-employment is under section 7A(1) or (3)(a)(i)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contract has been entered into by the employee and his or her employer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7A(4) the employer has complied with the requirement to enter into a re-employment contract` MEANS
    IF NOT `the re-employment is under section 7A(1) or (3)(a)(i)`
    THEN
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the requirement is "for the purposes of re-employment under subsection (1) or (3)(a)(i)"
        NOTHING
    ELSE IF `a contract has been entered into by the employee and his or her employer`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a re-employment contract must be entered into by the employee and his or her employer" -- a requirement not met (marginal reading (a))
            JUST FALSE

@ref s 7A(4) (src:401-405)
GIVEN `the re-employment is under section 7A(1) or (3)(a)(i)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7A(4) the job scope and the terms and conditions may vary from the previous contract` MEANS
    IF `the re-employment is under section 7A(1) or (3)(a)(i)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is "for the purposes of re-employment under subsection (1) or (3)(a)(i)"
        NOTHING

-- The Act's own examples are "the employee's productivity, performance, duties and responsibilities, and the wage
-- system such as the seniority system", and the list is "not limited to" them.  A factor the Act names counts as
-- reasonable; for any other factor, whether it is reasonable is an input.
-- src:409 | (5) Any variation referred to in subsection (4) must be based on
-- src:410 | reasonable factors such as, but not limited to, the employee’s
-- src:411 | productivity, performance, duties and responsibilities, and the wage
-- src:412 | system such as the seniority system applicable to the employee.
@ref s 7A(5) (src:409-412)
GIVEN factor IS A `Factor for a variation`
      `the other factor is reasonable` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7A(5) the variation is based on a reasonable factor` MEANS
    CONSIDER factor
    WHEN `the employee's productivity` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the employee's performance` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the employee's duties and responsibilities` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the wage system, such as the seniority system, applicable to the employee` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "reasonable factors such as, but not limited to" the four named; whether another factor is reasonable is not for the text to say
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any variation referred to in subsection (4) must be based on reasonable factors" -- a factor found not reasonable -- marginal reading (a)
    WHEN `another factor` THEN `the other factor is reasonable`

-- One year is counted from the first day of the period: a period of one year that begins on a day ends on the day before
-- the next anniversary of that day.  A period beginning on 29 February has no such anniversary in a year that is not a
-- leap year, and the Act does not say how to count (fork F18).
-- src:414 | (6) Unless otherwise agreed by the parties to a re-employment
-- src:415 | contract, the period of employment stipulated in the contract must not
-- src:416 | be less than one year at any one time.
@ref s 7A(6) (src:414-416)
GIVEN `the first day of the period of employment stipulated in the contract` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period of employment stipulated in the contract` IS A DATE
      `the parties agreed otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7A(6) the period of employment stipulated is not less than one year` MEANS
    IF `the parties agreed otherwise`
    THEN
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Unless otherwise agreed by the parties to a re-employment contract"; the section sets no minimum where the parties agreed otherwise and says nothing more of that case (fork F8)
        NOTHING
    ELSE IF DATE_MONTH `the first day of the period of employment stipulated in the contract` EQUALS 2 AND DATE_DAY `the first day of the period of employment stipulated in the contract` EQUALS 29
         THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a period that begins on 29 February has no anniversary a year later in a year that is not a leap year, and the Act does not say how to count one year from it
            NOTHING
         ELSE IF `the last day of the period of employment stipulated in the contract` AT LEAST (`add years` `the first day of the period of employment stipulated in the contract` 1 MINUS 1)
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE
                -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the period of employment stipulated in the contract must not be less than one year at any one time"
                JUST FALSE

-- src:420 | (7) Despite subsection (6), where the period between —
-- src:422 | (a) the start of re-employment under a re-employment contract
-- src:423 | for an employee; and
-- src:430 | (b) the date on which the employee attains the employee’s
-- src:431 | prescribed re-employment age,
-- src:433 | is less than one year, the period of employment under the
-- src:434 | re-employment contract may be for that shorter period.
@ref s 7A(7) (src:420-434) 
GIVEN `the first day of the period of employment stipulated in the contract` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period of employment stipulated in the contract` IS A DATE
      `the date the employee attains the prescribed re-employment age` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7A(7) the period of employment may be for the shorter period` MEANS
    IF `the date the employee attains the prescribed re-employment age` LESS THAN (`add years` `the first day of the period of employment stipulated in the contract` 1) AND `the last day of the period of employment stipulated in the contract` AT MOST (`the date the employee attains the prescribed re-employment age`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is for a re-employment whose period "between the start of re-employment ... and the date on which the employee attains the employee's prescribed re-employment age ... is less than one year"; the case falls outside
        NOTHING

§§ `Section 7A(9) to (11) -- retiring, and the prescribed re-employment age`

-- src:442 | (9) Despite any of the provisions of this Act, an eligible employee
-- src:443 | may retire or be retired, if he or she does not wish to be employed by
-- src:444 | his or her employer on or after the date the employee attains the
-- src:445 | specified age.
@ref s 7A(9) (src:442-445)
GIVEN `the employee is an eligible employee` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the employee does not wish to be employed by the employer on or after the date the employee attains the specified age` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7A(9) the eligible employee may retire or be retired` MEANS
    IF `the employee is an eligible employee` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the employee does not wish to be employed by the employer on or after the date the employee attains the specified age`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is "Despite any of the provisions of this Act" for "an eligible employee" who "does not wish to be employed by his or her employer on or after the date the employee attains the specified age"; the case falls outside, or eligibility is not known
        NOTHING

-- src:447 | (10) An eligible employee who intends to retire must, insofar as is
-- src:448 | reasonably practicable, give written notice to his or her employer,
-- src:449 | within a reasonable period before the employee retires, stating his or
-- src:450 | her intention to do so.
@ref s 7A(10) (src:447-450)
GIVEN `the employee is an eligible employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee intends to retire` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is reasonably practicable for the employee to give written notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee gave the employer written notice stating the intention to retire` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice was given within a reasonable period before the employee retires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7A(10) the employee has complied with the duty to give written notice of the intention to retire` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the employee is an eligible employee` AND `the employee intends to retire`)
    THEN
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is of "An eligible employee who intends to retire"
        NOTHING
    ELSE IF NOT `it is reasonably practicable for the employee to give written notice`
         THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is owed "insofar as is reasonably practicable"; where giving notice was not reasonably practicable the section does not say what is owed
            NOTHING
         ELSE IF `the employee gave the employer written notice stating the intention to retire` AND `the notice was given within a reasonable period before the employee retires`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE
                -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must ... give written notice to his or her employer, within a reasonable period before the employee retires, stating his or her intention to do so" -- a requirement not met (marginal reading (a))
                JUST FALSE

@ref s 7A(10) (src:447-450)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`s 7A(10) the eligible employee must give the employer written notice of the intention to retire` MEANS
    PARTY Employee
    MUST `give the employer written notice of the intention to retire`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Employee BECAUSE "s 7A(10): the employer was not given written notice of the intention to retire"

-- The Minister's range: "at least 67 years but not more than 70 years", by notification in the Gazette.
-- src:452 | (11) The Minister may, by notification in the Gazette, specify the
-- src:453 | prescribed re-employment age applicable to any class of employees,
-- src:454 | which must be at least 67 years but not more than 70 years.
@ref s 7A(11) (src:452-454)
GIVEN `the age specified` IS A NUMBER
      `the age is specified by notification in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7A(11) the age specified may be the prescribed re-employment age` MEANS
    IF `the age specified` LESS THAN 67 OR `the age specified` GREATER THAN 70
    THEN
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "which must be at least 67 years but not more than 70 years" -- a requirement read as closing the range (marginal reading (a))
        JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the age is specified by notification in the Gazette`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the Minister "may, by notification in the Gazette, specify"; the age is within the range but was not specified in that way
            NOTHING

§§ `Section 7B -- period of service under the previous contract and under the re-employment contract`

-- "Unless otherwise agreed by the parties ..., and subject to subsections (2) and (3)": the previous service is
-- disregarded for any right, privilege, obligation or liability, except as subsection (2) reckons it.  Where the
-- parties agreed otherwise, the "unless" takes the case out of the rule, and the answer is that the previous service is
-- not disregarded (fork F8); what the parties agreed in its place is theirs and is not for this function.
-- src:461 | 7B.—(1) Unless otherwise agreed by the parties to a contract of
-- src:462 | service, and subject to subsections (2) and (3), when a re-employment
-- src:463 | contract is entered into between an employer and an employee of the
-- src:464 | employer pursuant to section 7A(4), then for the purposes of
-- src:465 | determining any right, privilege, obligation or liability to be
-- src:466 | acquired, accrued or incurred by the employee under the
-- src:467 | employee’s re-employment contract, any period for which the
-- src:468 | employee has served under his or her employer under the previous
-- src:469 | contract of service before the employee commences his or her service
-- src:470 | under the re-employment contract is disregarded.
@ref s 7B(1) (src:461-470)
GIVEN `a re-employment contract is entered into pursuant to section 7A(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the parties to the contract of service agreed otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      purpose IS A `Purpose of reckoning service`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7B(1) the previous service is disregarded for the purpose` MEANS
    IF NOT `a re-employment contract is entered into pursuant to section 7A(4)`
    THEN
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section applies "when a re-employment contract is entered into between an employer and an employee of the employer pursuant to section 7A(4)"
        NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the parties to the contract of service agreed otherwise`
         THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless otherwise agreed by the parties to a contract of service, ... any period for which the employee has served ... is disregarded"; they agreed otherwise, so the earlier service is not disregarded (fork F8, marginal reading (a))
            JUST FALSE
         ELSE
            CONSIDER purpose
            WHEN `computing the minimum period of 3 months for entitlement to annual leave under section 88A(1) of the Employment Act 1968` THEN
                -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "subject to subsections (2) and (3)", and subsection (2): the previous service "is to be reckoned for the purposes of -- (a) computing the minimum period of 3 months for entitlement to annual leave" -- marginal reading (c)
                JUST FALSE
            WHEN `determining the period of service for entitlement to paid sick leave under section 89(1) and (2) of the Employment Act 1968` THEN
                -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "subject to subsections (2) and (3)", and subsection (2): the previous service "is to be reckoned for the purposes of -- (b) determining the period of service of an employee for entitlement to paid sick leave" -- marginal reading (c)
                JUST FALSE
            WHEN `determining another right, privilege, obligation or liability under the re-employment contract` THEN JUST TRUE

-- src:474 | (2) Any period for which an employee has served under his or her
-- src:475 | employer before the employee commences his or her service under
-- src:477 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 1/7/2022
-- src:478 | Retirement and Re-employment
-- src:480 | 2020 Ed. Act 1993 10
-- src:482 | the re-employment contract entered into pursuant to section 7A(4) is
-- src:483 | to be reckoned for the purposes of —
-- src:485 | (a) computing the minimum period of 3 months for
-- src:486 | entitlement to annual leave under section 88A(1) of the
-- src:487 | Employment Act 1968; and
-- src:489 | (b) determining the period of service of an employee for
-- src:490 | entitlement to paid sick leave under section 89(1) and (2)
-- src:491 | of the Employment Act 1968.
@ref s 7B(2) (src:474-491)
GIVEN `a re-employment contract is entered into pursuant to section 7A(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      purpose IS A `Purpose of reckoning service`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7B(2) the previous service is reckoned for the purpose` MEANS
    IF NOT `a re-employment contract is entered into pursuant to section 7A(4)`
    THEN
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the reckoning is of service "before the employee commences his or her service under the re-employment contract entered into pursuant to section 7A(4)"
        NOTHING
    ELSE
        CONSIDER purpose
        WHEN `computing the minimum period of 3 months for entitlement to annual leave under section 88A(1) of the Employment Act 1968` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `determining the period of service for entitlement to paid sick leave under section 89(1) and (2) of the Employment Act 1968` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `determining another right, privilege, obligation or liability under the re-employment contract` THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): subsection (2) reckons the service "for the purposes of" (a) and (b); it does not say that no other purpose is reckoned, and subsection (1) disregards it for the rest
            NOTHING

-- src:495 | (3) An employee’s continuity of employment under re-employment
-- src:496 | is not broken if his or her employer re-employs or renews the
-- src:497 | re-employment of the employee in accordance with section 7A(4).
@ref s 7B(3) (src:495-497)
GIVEN `the employer re-employs or renews the re-employment of the employee in accordance with section 7A(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7B(3) the employee's continuity of employment under re-employment is not broken` MEANS
    IF `the employer re-employs or renews the re-employment of the employee in accordance with section 7A(4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the rule is for the case where "his or her employer re-employs or renews the re-employment of the employee in accordance with section 7A(4)"
        NOTHING

§§ `Section 7C(1) -- Employment assistance payment or alternative employment`

-- "Section 7A does not apply if ... and (a) ... or (b) ...".  A failed "if" is read as: section 7A applies (fork F9).
-- src:503 | 7C.—(1) Section 7A does not apply if an employer (called in this
-- src:504 | section E1) is unable to re-employ an eligible employee in
-- src:505 | accordance with section 7A because E1 is unable to find a vacancy
-- src:506 | in E1’s establishment that is suitable for the eligible employee,
-- src:507 | despite making reasonable attempts to do so in accordance with the
-- src:508 | tripartite guidelines, and —
-- src:510 | (a) E1 offers an employment assistance payment to the
-- src:511 | eligible employee; or
-- src:513 | (b) during the eligible employee’s employment with E1 —
-- src:515 | (i) another employer (called in this section E2) offers to
-- src:516 | employ the eligible employee in lieu of E1; and
-- src:518 | (ii) the eligible employee accepts the offer.
@ref s 7C(1) (src:503-518)
GIVEN `E1 is unable to find a vacancy in E1's establishment that is suitable for the eligible employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `E1 made reasonable attempts to find one in accordance with the tripartite guidelines` IS A BOOLEAN
      `E1 offers an employment assistance payment to the eligible employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another employer, E2, offers to employ the eligible employee in lieu of E1 during the eligible employee's employment with E1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the eligible employee accepts the offer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7C(1) section 7A does not apply to the employer` MEANS
    IF `E1 is unable to find a vacancy in E1's establishment that is suitable for the eligible employee` AND `E1 made reasonable attempts to find one in accordance with the tripartite guidelines` AND (`E1 offers an employment assistance payment to the eligible employee` OR (`another employer, E2, offers to employ the eligible employee in lieu of E1 during the eligible employee's employment with E1` AND `the eligible employee accepts the offer`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Section 7A does not apply if" the employer is unable to find a suitable vacancy despite reasonable attempts "and" (a) or (b) -- a failed "if" is read as: section 7A applies (fork F9, marginal reading (a))
        JUST FALSE

§§ `Section 7C(2) -- when the eligible employee moves to E2`

-- "Subject to any modifications as may be prescribed" (the modifications are not among the sources).
-- src:522 | (2) Subject to any modifications as may be prescribed, where
-- src:523 | subsection (1)(b) applies —
-- src:525 | (a) E1’s re-employment obligations to the eligible employee
-- src:526 | are discharged immediately before the agreed date;
@ref s 7C(2) (src:522-526)
GIVEN `subsection (1)(b) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreed date` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7C(2) E1's re-employment obligations are discharged on the date` MEANS
    IF NOT `subsection (1)(b) applies`
    THEN
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the rule is for the case "where subsection (1)(b) applies"
        NOTHING
    ELSE
        CONSIDER `the agreed date`
        -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "agreed date" means a date specified in a consent form mentioned in section 7C(7); none is given
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST agreed THEN
            -- "immediately before the agreed date" is read as the end of the day before it, so that on the agreed date and after the obligations are discharged (fork F10)
            IF `the date asked about` AT LEAST agreed
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE
                -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the text says when E1's obligations are discharged, "immediately before the agreed date"; it does not say they are discharged earlier or that they are not
                NOTHING

-- src:528 | (b) any reference to an employer in section 7A or 7B(3), or to
-- src:529 | E1 in subsection (1), includes a reference to E2 from that
-- src:530 | agreed date; and
@ref s 7C(2) (src:528-530)
GIVEN `subsection (1)(b) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreed date` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7C(2) the reference to the employer includes E2 on the date` MEANS
    IF NOT `subsection (1)(b) applies`
    THEN
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the rule is for the case "where subsection (1)(b) applies"
        NOTHING
    ELSE
        CONSIDER `the agreed date`
        -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "agreed date" means a date specified in a consent form mentioned in section 7C(7); none is given
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST agreed THEN
            IF `the date asked about` AT LEAST agreed
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE
                -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the reference to the employer includes E2 "from that agreed date"; the date is before it
                NOTHING

-- src:537 | (c) E1’s re-employment obligations towards the eligible
-- src:538 | employee survive any unlawful dismissal by E1 of the
-- src:539 | eligible employee before the agreed date, but to the extent
-- src:540 | provided in paragraphs (a) and (b).
@ref s 7C(2) (src:537-540)
GIVEN `subsection (1)(b) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `E1 unlawfully dismissed the eligible employee before the agreed date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7C(2) E1's re-employment obligations survive an unlawful dismissal by E1` MEANS
    IF `subsection (1)(b) applies` AND `E1 unlawfully dismissed the eligible employee before the agreed date`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the rule is for the case "where subsection (1)(b) applies" and E1 dismisses the eligible employee unlawfully "before the agreed date"
        NOTHING

§§ `Section 7C(3) to (5) -- the employment assistance payment`

-- src:544 | (3) Despite subsection (1)(a), an employer is not required to offer
-- src:545 | any employment assistance payment to an eligible employee who
-- src:546 | informs his or her employer of the employee’s decision not to
-- src:547 | continue to be employed by that employer on or after the date the
-- src:548 | employee attains the specified age.
@ref s 7C(3) (src:544-548)
GIVEN `the employee is an eligible employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee informed the employer of the decision not to continue to be employed by that employer on or after the date the employee attains the specified age` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7C(3) the employer is not required to offer an employment assistance payment` MEANS
    IF `the employee is an eligible employee` AND `the employee informed the employer of the decision not to continue to be employed by that employer on or after the date the employee attains the specified age`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the exemption is for "an eligible employee who informs his or her employer of the employee's decision not to continue to be employed by that employer on or after the date the employee attains the specified age"
        NOTHING

-- "the employment assistance payment is -- (a) a single lump sum payment paid by an employer by the last day of employment
-- of the eligible employee; or (b) other mutually agreed arrangements".  The two are the forms the section names, and the
-- subsection says the payment "is" one or the other: a lump sum paid after the last day, with no other arrangement
-- agreed, is neither, and the answer is no, which is also what the duty below treats as a breach (fork F11).
-- src:552 | (4) Subject to subsection (5), the employment assistance payment
-- src:553 | is —
-- src:555 | (a) a single lump sum payment paid by an employer by the last
-- src:556 | day of employment of the eligible employee; or
-- src:558 | (b) other mutually agreed arrangements.
@ref s 7C(4) (src:552-558)
GIVEN `the date the single lump sum payment was paid` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the last day of employment of the eligible employee` IS A DATE
      `other mutually agreed arrangements were made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7C(4) the employment assistance payment is made in a form the section names` MEANS
    IF `other mutually agreed arrangements were made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE
        CONSIDER `the date the single lump sum payment was paid`
        WHEN JUST paid THEN
            IF paid AT MOST `the last day of employment of the eligible employee`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE
                -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the employment assistance payment is -- (a) a single lump sum payment paid by an employer by the last day of employment ... or (b) other mutually agreed arrangements"; a lump sum paid after the last day, with no other arrangement agreed, is neither (fork F11, marginal reading (a))
                JUST FALSE
        WHEN NOTHING THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no single lump sum has been paid and no other arrangement was mutually agreed, so there is as yet no payment to say which form it takes
            NOTHING

-- The lump sum as a regulative rule: paid by the last day of employment, which is the last day on which it is timely.
@ref s 7C(4) (src:552-558)
GIVEN `the last day of employment of the eligible employee` IS A DATE
      `the day the clock starts` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`s 7C(4) the employer must pay the employment assistance payment as a single lump sum by the last day of employment` MEANS
    PARTY Employer
    MUST `pay the employment assistance payment as a single lump sum`
    WITHIN (Day `the last day of employment of the eligible employee` MINUS Day `the day the clock starts`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Employer BECAUSE "s 7C(4)(a): the single lump sum was not paid by the last day of employment"

-- src:560 | (5) In determining the amount of employment assistance payment
-- src:561 | to be paid under this section, an employer must take into account the
-- src:562 | tripartite guidelines.
@ref s 7C(5) (src:560-562)
GIVEN `the employer took the tripartite guidelines into account in determining the amount` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7C(5) the employer has complied with the duty to take the tripartite guidelines into account` MEANS
    IF `the employer took the tripartite guidelines into account in determining the amount`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In determining the amount of employment assistance payment to be paid under this section, an employer must take into account the tripartite guidelines" -- a requirement not met (marginal reading (a))
        JUST FALSE

§§ `Section 7C(6) to (8) -- service under E1, the consent form, and Parts 4 and 5`

-- "reckoned only for the purposes of (a) ... and (b)": a closed list, so any other purpose is not reckoned.
