`s 7C(7) the consent form is prima facie proof of the matters mentioned in subsection (1)(b)` MEANS
    IF `a consent form is signified by E1, E2 and the eligible employee` AND `it is in the prescribed form and manner`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the proof is of "a consent form signified by E1, E2 and the eligible employee in the prescribed form and manner"; the prescribed form and manner are not among the sources
        NOTHING

-- src:591 | (8) To avoid doubt, the references to an eligible employee’s
-- src:592 | employer in Parts 4 and 5 include references to E2, where applicable.
@ref s 7C(8) (src:591-592)
GIVEN `section 7C(1)(b) applies, so that E2 is the eligible employee's employer` IS A BOOLEAN
